<title>USA: Express Scripts authorizes share buyback.</title>
<headline>Express Scripts authorizes share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Express Scripts Inc said Friday its board authorized the repurchase of up to 850,000 shares of its Class A common stock. No time limit was set.</p>
<p>The company, which provides managed prescription drug services, has about 8.6 million Class A common shares outstanding and 7.5 million Class B shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The Class B shares are held by NYLife Healthcare Management Inc, a subsidiary of New York Life Insurance Co.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
